## 🏗️ CLEAN ARCHITECTURE BREAKDOWN

### Data Flow (End-to-End)

```
Browser (Next.js)
    │
    ▼ HTTP REST (fetch)
FastAPI (port 8000)
    │
    ├── POST /api/runs           → Creates Run → asyncio.create_task(run_agent)
    ├── POST /api/runs/{id}/events → Stores Activity → Classifier → Optionally run_agent
    ├── GET  /api/runs           → Query PostgreSQL
    └── POST /api/supervisor/scenario → _fire_scenario_events (background coroutine)
    │
    ▼
agent/runtime.py::run_agent(run_id, wake_trigger)
    │
    ├── Loads Run + Supervisor + last 30 Activities (SQLAlchemy async)
    ├── Builds system prompt from templates (prompts.py)
    ├── Calls Groq API (LLM) ─── max 10 iterations
    │       └── Receives tool_calls → execute_tool() → logs Activity
    ├── If sleep requested → schedule_wake_up() → APScheduler DateTrigger
    └── If completion → _complete_run() → Groq for summary → status=completed
    │
    ▼
APScheduler (AsyncIOScheduler + SQLAlchemyJobStore)
    ├── Durable jobs in PostgreSQL (survive restarts)
    ├── DateTrigger fires → _wake_run() → run_agent()
    └── Periodic: check_expired_runs() every 5 min → auto-complete old runs
    │
    ▼
PostgreSQL
    ├── supervisors table
    ├── runs table (JSONB state, ARRAY instructions)
    ├── activities table (append-only audit log)
    └── apscheduler_jobs table (scheduler persistence)
```

