### 7. 🟡 MEDIUM — `asyncio.create_task()` Without Error Supervision

**Location:** [`runs.py`](file:///H:/Projects/Order%20Supervisor%20(POC)/backend/app/api/runs.py#L94), [`events.py`](file:///H:/Projects/Order%20Supervisor%20(POC)/backend/app/api/events.py#L147)

```python
asyncio.create_task(_run_agent_background(run.id, "run_start"))
```

`asyncio.create_task()` creates fire-and-forget tasks. If the task raises an exception and there is no `.add_done_callback()` attached, the error is silently swallowed (only logged if Python detects it during GC). There's no retry logic, no dead-letter queue.

